fit q ~ 0.24*X + 36.7     (q vs X: slope ~1 confirms q = Theta(X))
fit q ~ 0.17*log2(maxspeed) + 36.7   (q vs log2 max-speed)

(LB) every q in [2..X] divides some speed of S_X (so q<=X is danger-blocked): True
=> q(S_X) > X, and q(S_X) ~ nextprime(X) = Theta(X) = Theta(log max-speed). PROVES no uniform band.
   LRC discrepancy analogue of arXiv:2607.00876's tight all-scales log^{3/2} lower bound.
